# Voice Surveys Monorepo - Project-wide Rules

## Project Structure
- `apps/` - Frontend applications (React/TypeScript)
  - `live-chatter/` - Real-time audio chat application
  - `survey-hub/` - Survey management and analytics dashboard
- `services/` - Backend services (Python)
  - `livekit-agent/` - LiveKit audio processing service
- `packages/` - Shared packages and types
- `supabase/` - Database schema and edge functions

## General Guidelines
1. Follow TypeScript best practices for frontend code
2. Use Python type hints and follow PEP 8 for backend code
3. Maintain consistent naming conventions across all services
4. Use shared types from `packages/shared/` for cross-service communication
5. Follow the established monorepo structure and avoid creating new top-level directories

## Code Style
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Add comprehensive comments for complex logic
- Follow existing code patterns in each service
- Use proper error handling and logging

## Architecture Principles
- Keep services loosely coupled
- Use shared types for data contracts
- Maintain clear separation between frontend and backend concerns
- Follow the established API patterns in each service
